@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Lessons & Help"; }
<header class="help-hero"><div><p class="eyebrow">Lessons &amp; Help</p><h1>Make your story, one clear step at a time.</h1><p>My Africa, My Narrative helps you turn your own recordings, words and images into a short private documentary while keeping you in control of every source.</p></div><nav class="lesson-jumps" aria-label="Help topics"><a href="#before">Before you begin</a><a href="#record">1. Record</a><a href="#shape">2. Shape</a><a href="#make">3. Make</a><a href="#export">4. Export</a></nav></header>

<section id="before" class="surface help-section"><p class="eyebrow">Before you begin</p><h2>What you need</h2><div class="requirement-grid"><article><span aria-hidden="true">🎙</span><h3>Your voice</h3><p>A recording made in the app or a permitted MP3, WAV, M4A, WebM or WebA file.</p></article><article><span aria-hidden="true">▣</span><h3>A real visual</h3><p>At least one permitted photo or video that belongs with the story.</p></article><article><span aria-hidden="true">✓</span><h3>Permission</h3><p>Confirm honestly that you may use each source. Owner attestation is not independent verification.</p></article><article><span aria-hidden="true">◷</span><h3>A little time</h3><p>A preview may be short. A final documentary must contain 60–90 seconds of selected scenes.</p></article></div><div class="notice"><strong>Privacy:</strong> Sources are stored privately and are available only through authorised routes. Do not upload material you do not have permission to use.</div></section>

<section class="lesson-grid">
<article id="record" class="surface lesson-card"><div class="lesson-number">1</div><div><p class="eyebrow">Record</p><h2>Collect original sources</h2><ol><li>Create or open a project.</li><li>Record with your microphone, or upload an existing audio file.</li><li>Stop and review the recording.</li><li>Confirm permission and save it to Sources.</li><li>Add at least one photo or video for the picture.</li></ol><p class="lesson-result"><strong>Ready to continue when:</strong> Sources shows permitted audio and a permitted image or video.</p></div></article>
<article id="shape" class="surface lesson-card"><div class="lesson-number">2</div><div><p class="eyebrow">Shape</p><h2>Choose the words and scenes</h2><ol><li>Listen to your source recording.</li><li>Enter the words actually spoken and their start/end range.</li><li>Save the reviewed transcript.</li><li>Create scenes using original audio, a real visual and caption text.</li><li>Reorder scenes, review the cut and approve the exact revision.</li></ol><p><strong>Timing example:</strong> speech from 5 to 18 seconds uses mark in <code>5000</code> and mark out <code>18000</code>.</p><p class="lesson-result"><strong>Ready to continue when:</strong> the current revision contains scenes and is approved.</p></div></article>
<article id="make" class="surface lesson-card"><div class="lesson-number">3</div><div><p class="eyebrow">Make</p><h2>Plan with what is real</h2><ol><li>Add the equipment, people, locations, time and optional budget you actually have.</li><li>Describe availability or limits.</li><li>Mark a resource unavailable when circumstances change.</li><li>Check every scene has real visual coverage.</li></ol><p class="lesson-result"><strong>Important:</strong> the app should not invent people, locations, equipment or prices.</p></div></article>
<article id="export" class="surface lesson-card"><div class="lesson-number">4</div><div><p class="eyebrow">Export</p><h2>Preview, review and finish</h2><ol><li>Resolve every readiness message.</li><li>Queue a preview to test picture, original voice and captions.</li><li>Refresh while the durable Worker processes the job.</li><li>Open the PreviewVideo and Captions under Current artifacts.</li><li>For a 60–90 second approved cut, queue the 1080 × 1920 final.</li></ol><p><strong>Job meanings:</strong> Queued is waiting; Running is rendering; Succeeded has files; Failed shows an actionable reason.</p><p class="lesson-result"><strong>Artifacts:</strong> MP4 is the video. SRT is the subtitle file. They are tied to the exact approved revision.</p></div></article>
</section>

<section class="surface help-section"><p class="eyebrow">Quick answers</p><h2>Common questions</h2><details><summary>Why can’t I add a scene?</summary><p>A scene requires permitted audio, a permitted image/video and a valid range where the end is after the start and stays within the recording.</p></details><details><summary>Why can I preview but not export the final?</summary><p>The current approved cut must total 60–90 seconds before final export becomes available.</p></details><details><summary>What happens after I change a scene?</summary><p>The change creates a new immutable revision. Review and approve that new revision, then render it again.</p></details><details><summary>Does the app replace my voice?</summary><p>No. Export trims and uses your selected original recording. Corrected caption text remains separate from the recorded speech.</p></details></section>

@if (User.Identity?.IsAuthenticated == true) { <div class="help-cta"><a class="button-primary" asp-controller="Projects" asp-action="Index">Go to my projects</a></div> } else { <div class="help-cta"><a class="button-primary" asp-controller="Account" asp-action="Register">Create an account</a><a asp-controller="Account" asp-action="Login">Sign in</a></div> }
